    "created_at": "2026-03-12T21:42:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-12T21:42:33Z",
    "body": "> So now, according to the current spec, small.png must be loaded.\n\nNo, this is not correct. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#select-an-image-source-from-a-source-set says \n\n> In an [implementation-defined](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined) manner, choose one [image source](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#image-source) from sourceSet. Let selectedSource be this choice.\n\nAn implementation can decide to never downgrade the selected source, i.e. once you've selected `big.png 1000w` and loaded it, you stick with this selection (until a *larger* image is needed).\n\nThat said, it's intended that the image's size for the purpose of `sizes=auto` calculation to be stable before and after loading an image, which is why size containment is forced. I don't recall why \"concrete object size\" was used instead of the computed content box width, though.\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9493 changed how this works (but before also used concrete object width); points to https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9448",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
