    "created_at": "2026-10-07T17:44:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-07T17:44:04Z",
    "body": "\n> That said, it's intended that the image's size for the purpose of `sizes=auto` calculation to be stable before and after loading an image, which is why size containment is forced. I don't recall why \"concrete object size\" was used instead of the computed content box width, though.\n> \n\nYea that makes size containment insufficient because size containment does not affect the post-loading concrete size in the contain/cover cases.\n\nWe should probably go with the content box as suggested here and as implemented in blink.\nSeparately, we should find a way to allow authors better control so that they can load crisp images with `object-fit`, e.g. let them specify the natural aspect-ratio in advance.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
