    "created_at": "2026-10-07T18:49:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-07T18:49:54Z",
    "body": "Some more concrete proposal:\nWhy don't we use the `h` value (currently specced as `future-compat-h` as a hint for defining a natural aspect ratio?\nThen when selecting a source, we can take that together with `w` to mean the expected aspect ratio, and then use it in conjunction with the image's computed `object-fit` to compute a more appropriate source. This would still re-select a source if the `object-fit` changes, but only based on the aspect ratios in `srcset` and not based on the image content.\n\nWDYT?\n\ncc @austinh",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
