    "updated_at": "2026-10-08T07:59:23Z",
    "body": "To summarize the proposal:\n\n- `h` descriptor (currently ignored) is taken into account to compute a `source aspect ratio` before fetching. The source aspect ratio defaults to the image's width/height attributes for sources with no `h`.\n- In `loading=eager sizes=auto` mode, the `source aspect ratio` together with the computed `object-fit` and the `content box` are used to compute the `source concrete width` (which is the expected concrete size if the image content matches the descriptor).\n- In `loading=eager` mode, the 2D area and fit can be put directly in the `sizes` attribute, with a fallback after the comma: `<img sizes=\"cover 300px 100vh, 300px\">`\n- Changing the content box or `object-fit` are relevant mutation for selecting a new source. Changing the concrete size is not, as it can be affected by the image content.\n- The `source concrete width` can be used by the browser for source selection (though that's somewhat implementation defined)\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
