    "body": "> [@noamr](https://github.com/noamr) the width and height attributes set `aspect-ratio` in the UA stylesheet. I think the intent is indeed that they should be used to \"set\" the aspect ratio, and you can override the box dimensions with CSS.\n\n`aspect-ratio` doesn't help because it sets the container aspect ratio and not the image aspect ratio considering `object-fit`.\n\n> \n> We can maybe still add the `h` descriptor, but then I think the purpose should be to improve resource selection rather than only set aspect ratio.\n\nYes, the idea here is that `h` *only* improves source selection and doesn't affect the resulting aspect ratio.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
